+  publicly exports `ArenaArray`, `ArenaMap`, `CapacityError`,
+  `ArenaArrayIter`, `ArenaArrayIterMut`, and `ArenaMapIter`. None is
+  exported by the prelude. `CapacityError` is the unit-only public enum:
+
+  ```ember
+  pub enum CapacityError:
+      Full
+  ```
+
+  The canonical constructors are:
+
+  ```ember
+  @borrows(arena)
+  fn ArenaArray.with_capacity[T](
+      arena: Arena,
+      capacity: usize
+  ) -> ArenaArray[T]
+
+  @borrows(arena)
+  fn ArenaMap.with_capacity[K: Eq + Hash, V](
+      arena: Arena,
+      capacity: usize
+  ) -> ArenaMap[K, V]
+  ```
+
+  Both constructors return an empty container with `len() == 0` and the
+  requested maximum capacity, including when capacity is zero. The `arena`
+  parameter is shared/borrowed as in `[ARN-1]`; construction needs no
+  `mut arena`. The result carries the Arena's region through
+  `@borrows(arena)`. Container methods use `self` or `mut self` according
+  to ordinary observation/mutation and never mutate the Arena cursor.
+* `[ARN-5b]` **Capacity, failure, and stability.** The construction capacity
+  is the maximum number of stored entries. An operation that would add an
+  entry beyond capacity MUST return `Err(CapacityError.Full)` through its
+  specified `Result`; ordinary capacity exhaustion MUST NOT panic, allocate,
+  reallocate, modify the Arena cursor, invalidate an existing element view, or
+  partially modify the container. A replacement of an existing Map key does
+  not consume another capacity slot. Because the backing buffer never moves,
+  an element view remains storage-valid until that element is removed or the
+  supplying Arena region ends, subject to the ordinary borrow/liveness rules.
+* `[ARN-5c]` **`ArenaArray[T]` minimum API.** The canonical minimum API is:
+
+  ```ember
+  len(self) -> usize
+  capacity(self) -> usize
+  is_empty(self) -> bool
+  get(self, index: usize) -> Option[ref T]
+  get_mut(mut self, index: usize) -> Option[ref mut T]
+  push(mut self, owned value: T) -> Result[void, CapacityError]
+  insert(mut self, index: usize, owned value: T) -> Result[void, CapacityError]
+  remove(mut self, index: usize) -> Option[T]
+  clear(mut self) -> void
+  iter(self) -> ArenaArrayIter[T]
+  iter_mut(mut self) -> ArenaArrayIterMut[T]
+  ```
+
+  `ArenaArrayIter[T]` is an Arena-backed `@view` iterator implementing the
+  existing associated-type contract `Iterator[Item = ref T]`.
+  `ArenaArrayIterMut[T]` is an Arena-backed `@view` iterator implementing
+  `Iterator[Item = ref mut T]`. Iteration is in increasing index order and is
+  deterministic. Indexing and insertion indices follow ordinary
+  `Array`/`Span` bounds rules. `remove` moves out the removed value.
+* `[ARN-5d]` **`ArenaMap[K, V]` minimum API.** `ArenaMap[K, V]` requires
+  `K: Eq + Hash`, using the same equality/hash contract as ordinary
+  `Map[K, V]`. Its canonical minimum API is:
